    "object": {
      "Graph": {
        "@Type": "f8a58466",
        "@Value": {
          "Implementation": {
            "@Type": "3b83b776",
            "@Value": {
              "TextDocument": {
                "@Type": "f3878285",
                "@Value": {
                  "TextBlobForSerialisation": "(string)IF 1 <= head AND head <= CONS_HEAP_SIZE THEN\n\tcell := ADR(heap[head]);\n\tfind := TRUE;\nELSE\n\tfind := FALSE;\nEND_IF\n",
                  "LineInfoPersistence": "(string)7f64d0c3-9ff9-4531-bf6d-77bf2ec41870_Impl_LineIds"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "Interface": {
            "@Type": "a9ed5b7e",
            "@Value": {
              "TextDocument": {
                "@Type": "f3878285",
                "@Value": {
                  "TextBlobForSerialisation": "(string)(*\n================================================================================\nFunction Block Method : ConsHeap.find\n\nPurpose:\n    Finds a cell in the heap by register.\n\nApplication:\n    Use to retrieve a cell and validate its register before reading or writing.\n\nOperation:\n    1. Checks whether head is between 1 and CONS_HEAP_SIZE inclusive.\n    2. Copies the heap cell to the output cell when the register is valid.\n\nInputs:\n    head - Register to check.\n\nOutputs:\n    cell - Cell value; valid only when find returns TRUE.\n\nInOut:\n    None.\n\nReturn Value:\n    BOOL - TRUE when head is a valid heap register; otherwise FALSE.\n\nAssumptions:\n    - CONS_HEAP_SIZE matches the upper bound of heap.\n\nLimitations:\n    - content is not assigned when cr is invalid.\n\nDependencies:\n    - heap.\n    - CONS_HEAP_SIZE.\n\nExample:\n\n    xValid := fbConsHeap.find(head := registerOfCell, cell => copyOfCell);\n\nRevision History:\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Date         Version  Author           Description\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    13/11/2026   1.0      CannyIEC         Documented existing behaviour\n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n================================================================================\n*)\nMETHOD find : BOOL\nVAR_INPUT\n\thead : CONS_REG;\nEND_VAR\nVAR_OUTPUT\n\tcell : POINTER TO ConsCell;\nEND_VAR\n",
                  "LineInfoPersistence": "(string)7f64d0c3-9ff9-4531-bf6d-77bf2ec41870_Decl_LineIds"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "TypeInfos": {
        "3b83b776": "{3b83b776-fb25-43b8-99f2-3c507c9143fc}",
